### Description

following [this](https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/foundations/prompts#example-assistant-message-with-tool-call) and seems like `CoreMesssage` or `UIMessage` miss the `type` field. Or does the latest version not align with the docs? Can someone clear the air?

### Code example

```ts
const { text, toolResults, toolCalls } = await generateText({
  model,
  messages: [
    { role: 'user', content: 'hello' },
    {
      role: 'assistant',
      content: 'Hello',
    },
    { role: 'user', content: 'show me my account please' },
    {
      type: 'tool-call', // ⛔️ Object literal may only specify known properties, and 'type' does not exist in type 'UIMessage'
      toolCallId: 'call_f7bsXvQFhv8tjEZdUjHah42v',
      toolName: 'showMyAccount',
      args: {},
    },
    { role: 'user', content: 'thanks g' },
  ],
});
```

EDIT:

found `CoreToolMessage` and it looks like:
```ts
type CoreToolMessage = {
    role: 'tool';
    content: ToolContent;
    /**
  Additional provider-specific metadata. They are passed through
  to the provider from the AI SDK and enable provider-specific
  functionality that can be fully encapsulated in the provider.
   */
    experimental_providerMetadata?: ProviderMetadata;
};
```

Please update the docs.

### AI provider

@ai-sdk/openai ^1.1.2

